# work.Tool is the Api over providers the binary chooses; package work
# sees no provider of its contracts. The Api's law runs in package memory
# under overTool (a Tool over the memory providers) and overClient.
# workapi's Client is the Api over a send function, which no generator
# builds; the law runs in memory under overClient (a Client whose send is
# Call on a memory Tool). A workapi test cannot bind one: memory imports workapi.
skip law work.Api.NewIsListedOnce for Client: Client is built only by its constructor NewClient, which takes a value a case cannot draw; a value drawn from its fields may be one NewClient refuses
skip law Api.NewIsListedOnce for Tool: Tool is built only by its constructor NewTool, which takes a value a case cannot draw; a value drawn from its fields may be one NewTool refuses
# The host Cloners (btrfs, reflink, clonefile, copy) run system commands
# through an exec.Runner, which no generator builds. Their laws run under
# each package's onHost context instead, over exec.NewTestHost in a folder
# of each case's own (TestAmbient), and in package memory against the
# model. clonefile's laws run cp -c for real only on macOS with APFS;
# elsewhere a clone is Unsupported and they hold by their failure cases.
skip law work.Cloner.CloneMakesTheTree for Cloner: its values have no generator: system.Trees has an unexported field, so only package system builds it; use system.New; a func NewCloner() Cloner with no rows would build one for each case
skip law work.Cloner.DiscardDiscards for Cloner: its values have no generator: system.Trees has an unexported field, so only package system builds it; use system.New; a func NewCloner() Cloner with no rows would build one for each case
