# journal.Lock takes the host's file locks through an fs.Host, which no
# generator builds. The law runs under journal's onHost context (fs.LockFile
# in each case's folder) and against memory's shared locks;
# runtime/v1 TestFSLockFileExcludes holds the lock's exclusion, and
# scripts/workrace races two processes on it.
skip law work.Lock.HoldExcludes for Lock: its values have no generator: fs.Host has an unexported field, so only package fs builds it; use fs.NewTestHost or fs.NewHost; a func NewLock() Lock with no rows would build one for each case
